# Licensing

This repository is dual-licensed. Which license applies depends on what you are
using.

| Content | License | File |
|---|---|---|
| Code, scripts, configuration, Dockerfiles, YAML | Apache License 2.0 | `LICENSE-code` |
| Prose: runbooks, troubleshooting entries, chapters, diagrams | CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 | `LICENSE-prose` |

## Plain-language summary

**Code** — use it for anything, including commercially. Keep the attribution and
the `NOTICE` file.

**Prose** — you may share and adapt it, including remixing it into your own
work, provided you (a) credit the author, (b) do not use it commercially, and
(c) license your adaptation under the same terms.

"Non-commercial" is aimed squarely at one behaviour: scraping open technical
writing and reselling it as a padded ebook. It is not intended to obstruct
teaching, internal corporate use, conference talks, blog posts, or study
groups.

## Commercial use of the prose

If you want to use the prose commercially — training materials you charge for,
a book, paid courseware, redistribution inside a commercial product — that is
usually fine, but it needs a separate license. Open an issue or contact the
author. This is a conversation, not a refusal.

## Rights reserved by the author

The author is the sole copyright holder and retains the right to publish
commercial editions of this material, including print and ebook editions. The
licenses above govern third-party use; they do not constrain the author.

See `docs/decisions/` for the reasoning behind this arrangement.
